Marcus pulled up the integration schedule. "We're planning graduated deployment.
Facility systems rst, then local infrastructure, then regional integration. Full
operational capability by month six."
"That's too slow."
Marcus paused. "Ma'am?"
"General, I supported this appropriation because you convinced me AGI could help
solve existential problems. But existential problems have timelines. Climate
cascade points are approaching. Infrastructure is degrading faster than we can

maintain it. We don't have a year for graduated deployment.""Senator, rushing deployment
increases risk—"
"And delaying deployment guarantees failure. General, I've seen the models. The
ones you showed us in classied brieng. We have maybe ten years before cascade
