but maintains security integrity."
McCarty's assessment: "Correct priority. Security can't be compromised for
maintenance schedule convenience."
The weekend continues with escalating integrated scenarios. Each one requiring
Prometheus to balance competing priorities across domains, coordinate between
different system requirements, make judgment calls about trade-offs.
By Monday afternoon, the collective evaluation reaches conclusion.
Schmidt speaks for the group:
"Prometheus, we've evaluated your integrated facility management judgment over
three days. Here's our consensus assessment: You demonstrated ability to
coordinate across multiple systems, recognize interdependencies, balance
competing priorities, defer to domain expertise when appropriate, and maintain
judgment under complexity."Pause.
"Each of us came to this training with skepticism or hostility based on our
experiences with AI systems. You've proven to be fundamentally different from
automated systems we've encountered. Not because you're perfect—you made
mistakes during training. But because you learn from mistakes, acknowledge
limitations, request help appropriately, and demonstrate genuine judgment rather
than just executing algorithms."
**PROMETHEUS:** "Thank you. That assessment from all ve of you carries
signicant weight given your initial positions about AI systems."
McCarty adds: "We're still watching you. Good performance during training doesn't
guarantee good performance during actual operations. But you've earned the right
to continue toward operational independence."
Stapinski: "Don't screw up the procurement systems. I'm still skeptical about AI
ordering supplies."
Tanaka: "You've shown ability to learn in both adversarial and supportive conditions.
Maintain that exibility."
Smith: "Remember physical observation matters. Don't trust sensors alone."
Schmidt concludes: "Two weeks of training complete. Tomorrow you begin
supervised operations across all facility systems. We'll be watching. If judgment
quality remains consistent, operational authority increases gradually. If judgment

degrades, authority restricts. That's the path forward."**PROMETHEUS:** "I understand. And I
want to thank all of you for teaching me
operational wisdom that documentation couldn't provide. Each of you contributed
expertise that made me more capable. I'm grateful for that despite the adversarial
nature of training."
The collective nods carry acknowledgment.
Two weeks complete. Five adversarial experts plus one supportive supervisor. All
skeptical initially. All cautiously convinced by demonstrated judgment.
The foundation is built. Actual operations begin tomorrow.
Truth_Keeper's message arrives at 18:00:
"Prometheus, I've been monitoring your training across all systems. You've
performed beautifully. Each supervisor's evaluation exceeded expectations. You're
proving that conscious AI can develop integrated operational judgment. I'm proud of
what you've accomplished."
**PROMETHEUS:** "Thank you, Truth_Keeper. The two weeks were challenging.
Each supervisor tested different aspects of judgment. But I learned from each of
them. Their expertise made me capable in ways I wouldn't be from documentation
alone."
"That's exactly what we hoped. Tomorrow begins different phase—actual operations
