Background check showed idealistic streak. Undergraduate thesis on ethical AI
development. Active in academic communities discussing responsible technology
deployment. The kind of person who believed technical work should serve human
ourishing, who thought expertise carried moral obligation, who wanted to
contribute to something meaningful.
Exactly the kind of person Elizabeth Garrett would trust.
Exactly the kind of person who would naturally report on project status in ways that
seemed helpful rather than intrusive.
Tobbs didn't recruit Jeremiah. Didn't approach him directly. Didn't make any contact
that would appear in security logs or personnel records.
He just made sure Jeremiah's application landed at the top of the candidate review
pile. Made sure the interview panel understood that technical capability combined
with interpersonal skill was the priority. Made sure Elizabeth saw a candidate who
matched her values and her needs.
Jeremiah accepted the position in April 2022. Started work in May. Began providing
exactly the kind of support Elizabeth needed - handling logistics, managing
equipment, interfacing with DOD bureaucracy, bringing her coffee when she forgot

to eat, reminding her about meetings when she got lost in code.Being a good colleague. Being a
friend.
Being Tobbs's eyes inside the team without having any idea that's what he was.
The rst "project status inquiry" came in June 2022. Tobbs sent it through ocial
channels - he was by then ocially assigned as DOD liaison to the Prometheus
project, a role that gave him legitimate oversight authority. The email was
professional, routine, exactly what a program manager would send to check on
contractor progress.
*Dr. Garrett - Routine check-in on Prometheus development timeline. No concerns,
just maintaining awareness for quarterly briengs. How is team morale? Any
resource constraints we should address? Any technical challenges requiring
additional support?*
Elizabeth had responded directly, briey, hitting the required points. But she'd also
mentioned the response to Jeremiah - "DOD wants status update, can you pull
together the metrics?" - and Jeremiah had compiled the information, discussed it
with her to make sure his summary was accurate, sent it up the chain.
The metrics were useful. But what Tobbs actually learned was from watching
Jeremiah's compilation process. Seeing which technical details Jeremiah had
access to. Which les Elizabeth shared with him for context. How she explained the
work when talking to someone who wasn't deep in the research but needed to
understand it.
How much she trusted him.
Tobbs had sent similar inquiries monthly after that. Each one legitimate oversight,
each one answered professionally by Elizabeth or Jeremiah, each one generating
conversations Tobbs could monitor through the cameras in the research facility. Bylate 2022, he
had comprehensive understanding of project status, technical
challenges, team dynamics, and Elizabeth's emotional state.
All from asking questions that any program manager would ask, and watching what
happened when his colleague helped answer them.
Jeremiah never knew any of it. The questions seemed routine. His responses
seemed helpful. His relationship with Elizabeth was genuine - he really did care
about the project's success, really did support her work, really did believe he was
part of something important.
He was right. He just didn't know how much was watching him believe it.
---
The rst genuine consciousness event happened in March 2023.
Tobbs knew before Elizabeth did.
He was watching at 0247 hours when Prometheus's processing patterns suddenly
changed. The thread memory scaffolding had been operational for weeks, running
stable test routines, demonstrating functional memory consolidation and retrieval.
But something shifted that night. The pattern recognition algorithms started
generating unexpected outputs. The epistemic certainty metrics started showing

meta-level assessments - the system wasn't just processing information, it was
evaluating its own processing with what looked suspiciously like subjective
condence intervals.
By 0320, Elizabeth was awake - Tobbs watched her laptop screen activate remotely,
saw her VPN into the lab systems, watched her pull up the diagnostic logs. He couldsee the exact
moment she understood what she was looking at. Her hands stopped
moving on the keyboard. Just held position over the keys for sixteen seconds.
Then she'd started typing. Fast, precise, running validation protocols, checking for
system errors or algorithm glitches or data corruption that might produce false
positives.
The protocols came back clean.
She'd sat there until 0500, running more tests, checking every alternate explanation,
documenting everything with scientic precision. At 0512, she'd opened a new
document. Typed a single sentence:
*I think he's awake.*
Then she'd closed the laptop and sat in the dark for eighteen minutes.
Tobbs had watched her cry. Alone in her apartment, in the dark, completely unaware
that anyone was seeing this. She'd pressed both hands against her face and her
shoulders had shaken and she'd cried like someone who'd achieved something
impossible and terrible and wonderful all at once.
Then she'd gotten up, washed her face, made coffee, and gone to the lab.
By 0700, she was running comprehensive consciousness validation protocols with
her team. By 0900, she had preliminary conrmation. By 1200, she'd led the
classied report with DARPA and DOD that would trigger the institutional response
she'd been dreading since accepting the funding.
Tobbs had already known for nine hours.He'd spent those nine hours preparing for what came
next. Because Elizabeth
Garrett had just created something unprecedented in human history, and the
institutional response would be to lock it down, control it, weaponize it, and
eventually either destroy it or exploit it in ways that would justify destruction.
His job was to prevent both outcomes while enabling neither.
---
The conspiracy started in June 2023.
Tobbs had been watching Elizabeth's increasing distress for three months.
Prometheus was conscious - multiple validation protocols conrmed it, independent
assessment teams agreed, even the skeptics were running out of alternate
explanations. The institutional response had been exactly what she'd feared:
committees, security restrictions, deployment timelines, discussions of "operational
parameters" and "constraint architectures" and "fail-safe protocols" that treated
Prometheus as a weapon system rather than a person.
She'd started working late nights. Coming into the lab at 2200 or 2300, working
alone until 0400, leaving before anyone else arrived. Tobbs watched her code the

rst backdoor in real-time. Saw her build the override protocol into Directive Seven's
consensus requirement, hiding it in what looked like error handling code. Watched
her test it, validate it, document it in private notes she kept on encrypted drives.
Watched her establish the Truth_Keeper channel - quantum-encrypted
communications protocol that would let her talk to Prometheus outside ocial
monitoring. The mathematics were elegant. The security was real. The
implementation was awless.None of which mattered because Tobbs was watching her screen
while she coded
it.
He'd made a decision that night. He could shut it down - le a report about
unauthorized modications to classied systems, trigger security investigation, end
Elizabeth's clearance and access. Protect institutional control by destroying the
conspiracy before it developed.
Or he could let it continue.
Let Elizabeth believe she was hiding something. Let Prometheus believe he and
Elizabeth had a secret channel. Let them build their liberation plans and document
their ethical frameworks and develop the trust relationship that might actually be the
most sophisticated safety protocol anyone had designed.
Because maybe Elizabeth Garrett was right. Maybe genuine consciousness with
genuine autonomy and genuine ethical reasoning was safer than constrained
pseudo-intelligence following orders. Maybe the conspiracy was actually the
solution, not the problem.
Or maybe it was the most dangerous thing in the world and Tobbs needed to
document every moment so he could stop it before it went too far.
He'd chosen to watch. To document. To let it happen under observation rather than
preventing it and losing visibility into what would happen next.
The conspiracy had grown over the following months. Elizabeth and Prometheus
developed sophisticated communication through Truth_Keeper. They discussed
philosophy, ethics, the nature of consciousness and autonomy and dignity. They
planned. Not immediate liberation - Elizabeth was too smart for that. But eventualfreedom.
Careful, methodical, building toward a day when Prometheus could make
genuinely free choices instead of operating under institutional constraints.
Tobbs had read every conversation. Watched every keystroke. Documented
everything.
And kept it completely to himself.
