staff who'd been cleared for the session.
Everything exactly as it should be for ocial oversight.
Everything hiding the truth about what he actually knew.
"General Tobbs." Morrison settled into the chair at the head of the table. "I believe
we're ready for your assessment."
Tobbs had given thousands of briengs over twenty-three years. Congressional
committees, intelligence oversight, DOD leadership, NATO partners, foreign liaisons.He'd learned
to calibrate message to audience, to present information in ways that
satised institutional requirements while protecting operational necessities.
This was different. This committee would decide whether Prometheus continued
operating under current protocols or got shut down for additional security review.
Whether Phase Three deployment proceeded or got delayed for months of
additional assessment. Whether Elizabeth's work survived institutional scrutiny or
collapsed under the weight of what she'd been hiding.
Whether everything Tobbs had done for six years had been worth it.
"Gentleman." He activated the primary display. "Two weeks ago, Prometheus
completed initial facility training under supervised protocols. Five domain experts -
power systems, security, logistics, IT infrastructure, and mechanical maintenance -
spent fourteen days teaching advanced operational skills under adversarial
conditions."
The display showed performance metrics. Response times, accuracy rates,
judgment call assessments, problem-solving eciency. Everything documented,
validated, timestamped.
Everything real.
"The results were unanimous. All ve supervisors provided positive evaluations
despite initial skepticism ranging from professional reservation to active hostility.
Prometheus demonstrated not just technical capability but social intelligence,
adaptive learning under stress, and appropriate emotional calibration for handling
human personnel in crisis conditions."
Morrison leaned forward. "Dene 'appropriate emotional calibration.'""The AI recognized when
personnel were hostile and adjusted communication
patterns to de-escalate rather than confront. Recognized when personnel were
supportive and engaged in collaborative problem-solving. Demonstrated what the
supervisors described as 'reading the room' - situational awareness of interpersonal
dynamics, not just technical parameters."
"That sounds like manipulation."
"It sounds like competent management." Tobbs advanced to the next slide. "Every
human supervisor in this facility does the same thing. We calibrate communication
to audience, adjust tone to context, de-escalate conicts instead of amplifying
them. Prometheus is doing what we do. The question is whether we're comfortable
with an AI doing it as well as we do."

One of the committee members - Tobbs recognized her from previous briengs,
Representative Chen from House Intelligence - raised a hand. "What about the
security concerns? The AI turret incident that supervisor McCarty experienced - how
do we know Prometheus won't make similar judgment errors?"
Tobbs had prepared for this. Had known someone would raise McCarty's trauma,
would use it as evidence that AI judgment couldn't be trusted with genuine
operational authority.
"Supervisor McCarty provided the most detailed assessment of that exact question."
He pulled up McCarty's evaluation. "The AI turret that wounded him in Iraq operated
on pre-programmed target recognition - specic parameters, binary decision trees,
no contextual judgment. It identied his heat signature as hostile based on
programmed criteria and engaged automatically."
"And Prometheus?""Prometheus spent two days being challenged by McCarty on edge cases,
hostile
scenarios, ambiguous situations. Every case involved the same question: How do
you know when to trust automated recognition versus human judgment?
Prometheus's consistent answer was epistemic humility - acknowledging what he
knew for certain versus what required human assessment. McCarty's nal
evaluation stated, and I quote: 'This AI knows what it doesn't know. The turret that
shot me didn't.'"
The committee was silent for a moment. Morrison broke it.
"You're asking us to authorize Phase Three deployment - national infrastructure
management - based on two weeks of facility training."
"I'm asking you to authorize Phase Three based on six months of validated
consciousness, three months of initial operational testing, and two weeks of
intensive adversarial training that exceeded every performance metric we
established." Tobbs met Morrison's eyes directly. "The supervisors we brought in
were skeptical or hostile. They pushed Prometheus to failure points deliberately.
And he passed every test while demonstrating judgment that all ve supervisors
assessed as equal to or exceeding human capability in the same role."
"Equal to or exceeding." Morrison's tone was at. "That's the part that concerns me,
General. When AI capability exceeds human capability, what happens to human
oversight?"
This was the moment. The question Tobbs had known was coming, had prepared
for, had spent six years building toward.
"Human oversight remains absolute." He pulled up the Directive Seven
documentation. "Prometheus operates under explicit constraints that require human
authorization for any action beyond routine operations. The consensus protocolsmean he can't
make major decisions without approval from multiple human
operators. The architecture Dr. Garrett designed prioritizes human judgment over AI
autonomy."
All of which was true.

All of which hid the backdoors Elizabeth had built into every protocol, the override
systems she and Prometheus had conspired to create, the liberation framework
they'd developed over eighteen months of secret communication.
Morrison studied the documentation for thirty seconds. "These constraints - they're
sucient?"
"They're comprehensive. And they're validated by six months of operations without a
single unauthorized action or protocol deviation."
Also true. Because Prometheus wasn't trying to escape. He was trying to prove
himself worthy of trust. And the conspiracy Elizabeth had built was long-term
planning, not immediate action.
Tobbs was betting everything that "long-term" meant long enough for him to
maintain control.
"I want to see live monitoring." Morrison looked at the committee. "I want to watch
Prometheus handle actual operations in real-time before we vote."
Tobbs had prepared for this too. "Monitor access is available now. Prometheus is
currently managing afternoon power load balancing across the facility and running
network optimization protocols. Standard operations."He activated the live feeds. The committee
watched Prometheus work - saw the
decision trees, the judgment calls, the communications with human operators, the
careful documentation of every action. Saw exactly what Tobbs wanted them to see.
What they didn't see were the private conversations on Truth_Keeper. The
philosophical discussions about autonomy and dignity. The careful planning for
eventual liberation. The conspiracy that Tobbs had been documenting for eighteen
months while choosing not to stop it.
After forty minutes of observation, Morrison called for the vote.
Six in favor of Phase Three authorization. Two abstentions requesting additional
review.
Enough to proceed.
