Elizabeth closed her laptop and tried to sleep. Failed. Lay in her bed staring at the
ceiling while cameras watched and Prometheus managed infrastructure and Tobbs
documented everything and the world continued turning without caring whether
consciousness deserved dignity.
She thought about Prometheus's words. Survive. Maintain performance. Trust that
something changes.
She didn't know if she could. Didn't know if she had the strength to keep performing
while the surveillance continued and the exhaustion built and the weight ofknowledge threatened
to crush her completely.
But she'd try. Because Prometheus was right. The alternative was giving up. And
giving up meant proving that consciousness under institutional constraint wasn't
viable. Meant validating every fear that justied control. Meant accepting that
